---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../lib/seo/site';

const title = 'Prototype and Pilot Terms of Use';
const description =
  'Terms for accessing Advanced Analytica prototype and pilot systems before production release.';

const page = {
  title,
  description,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/legal/prototype-pilot-terms`,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
    { name: 'Legal', url: `${SITE_URL}/legal/terms` },
    { name: 'Prototype and Pilot Terms', url: `${SITE_URL}/legal/prototype-pilot-terms` }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} page={page}>
  <section class="container-narrow py-16">
    <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-ink">Prototype and Pilot Terms of Use</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p><strong>Last updated: 9 August 2026.</strong></p>

      <p>
        These terms apply when Advanced Analytica Ltd gives you access to a
        client-facing prototype, proof of concept, pilot, beta, or other
        pre-production system. They are intended to set expectations clearly
        before a test flow is used.
      </p>

      <h2>Prototype status</h2>
      <p>
        Prototype and pilot systems are pre-production. They may be incomplete,
        unavailable, changed, suspended, or withdrawn without the same notice,
        service levels, continuity arrangements, or operational guarantees that
        would apply to a production service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outputs may contain errors, omissions, incomplete analysis, unexpected
        behaviour, or experimental features. You should treat all outputs as
        test material unless Advanced Analytica has separately agreed otherwise
        in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>Use during the test period</h2>
      <p>
        You use prototypes and pilots at your own risk during the agreed test
        period. They are provided for evaluation, workflow validation, user
        feedback, and technical proving only. They should not be relied on as a
        final approval, legal sign-off, compliance decision, or production
        business process.
      </p>

      <h2>Data processed</h2>
      <p>
        The categories of data processed will depend on the particular
        engagement, but may include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>identity and contact details, such as name, work email address, and company;</li>
        <li>authentication and access records, including magic-link requests and consent events;</li>
        <li>submitted test materials, creative assets, files, images, copy, or related notes;</li>
        <li>submission metadata, such as activity dates, content type, and selected workflow options;</li>
        <li>technical logs needed to operate, secure, debug, and improve the prototype.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For the Disney MagiKit Trailblazer pilot, this includes the test user's
        email address and the uploaded creative image or file that is held
        temporarily so the pilot workflow can process the submission.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability, data handling, and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Prototype infrastructure, monitoring, retention, recovery, audit, and
        data-handling processes may not yet match production standards. Advanced
        Analytica will use reasonable measures appropriate to the test, but the
        purpose of the pilot is to validate and improve the system before it is
        treated as production-ready.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pilot data should be retained only for as long as reasonably necessary
        for the relevant test, review, troubleshooting, governance, and legal
        purposes, unless a separate agreement or legal requirement applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Consent record</h2>
      <p>
        Access to a prototype or pilot may require an active acknowledgement of
        these terms. Where that happens, Advanced Analytica may record the
        consent event against the relevant user record, including the timestamp,
        policy version, engagement, and email address used for access.
      </p>

      <h2>Data protection</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are a liability and expectations caveat only. They do not
        override Advanced Analytica's obligations under UK GDPR, the Data
        Protection Act 2018, or any other applicable data protection law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lawful basis, purpose limitation, retention limits, security
        requirements, transparency duties, processor or controller obligations,
        and individual rights continue to apply in full regardless of prototype
        or pilot status.
      </p>

      <h2>Relationship with other terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms sit alongside any written agreement, statement of work,
        data processing agreement, or project-specific pilot terms agreed with
        Advanced Analytica. If a signed agreement sets a higher standard for a
        particular engagement, that agreement will continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about a prototype or pilot, including how data is
        handled in a specific engagement, please contact Advanced Analytica via
        the <a href="/company/contact">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
